Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: upstream, https://git.ffmpeg.org/gitweb/ffmpeg.git/commit/67241d1128c88269a3a3af378eaac165d0156187
From 67241d1128c88269a3a3af378eaac165d0156187 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:36:08 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 16/48] avcodec/h2645_sei: decode the multiview and depth
 information SEI messages

Decode every multiview and depth information SEI message of H.264
(multiview scene information 39, multiview acquisition information 40,
multiview view position 46, depth representation information 50, depth
timing 52, depth sampling information 53, constrained depth parameter set
identifier 54, alternative depth information 181; Annexes G, H and I)
and H.265 (depth representation information 177, multiview scene
information 178, multiview acquisition information 179, multiview view
position 180, alternative depth information 181; Annexes G and I) into
the frame side data of libavutil/multiview.h, with the checks of their
semantics. A reserved depth_representation_type keeps only the type, as
decoders ignore the data that follows it (G.14.3.4, H.13.2.3), and an
alternative depth information message with a reserved depth_type is
ignored (I.14.3.3).

With per_view_depth_timing_flag, a depth timing message holds one offset
for each of the NumDepthViews depth views of the MVCD sequence parameter
set, which the decoder does not read: the offsets the payload holds are
taken.

Add the functions the decoders keep the information in force with: each
message replaces the information of its type, and the information of the
types not received ends with its coded video sequence.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
